 - **Zoom bar.** The context window as a thin strip whose small slice widens into the skill list's bar. Each skill is one piece as wide as what was sent, grey to brand orange by its size against the largest on the first side (`--heat`); the names are one grey piece. A 2 px line marks the limit with its flag ("Limit: 8,000 characters"). The part past the line is hatched amber (`--hatch`, light and dark values) and labelled "Over the limit: not sent" ("cut off" for Codex); room left says "Free". A redraw moves each piece from where it was in 240 ms.
-- **Two sides.** Two panels of skill pills, the second dimmer with a hatched mark (Cursor's mark is a plain outline). A pill shows the name and its size. On the first side its line, fill and size warm from grey to brand orange with the same heat as its piece, so the largest descriptions stand out; the second side stays grey. The skill whose Details show has an ink ring (an ink piece), never orange. A pill the tray changes has a dashed line; after Apply, a skill that gets its description is filled and one that loses it has an amber line. A skill on no side sits apart below. Pointing at a pill or a piece lights both.
+- **Two sides.** Two panels of skill pills, the second dimmer with a hatched mark (Cursor's mark is a plain outline). A pill shows the name and its size; a cut one shows how much was sent ("342 of 570"). On the first side its line, fill and size warm from grey to brand orange with the same heat as its piece, so the largest descriptions stand out; the second side stays grey. The skill whose Details show has an ink ring (an ink piece), never orange. A pill the tray changes has a dashed line; after Apply, a skill that gets its description is filled and one that loses it has an amber line. A skill on no side sits apart below. Pointing at a pill or a piece lights both.
 - **Details.** A skill opens the floating Details with its size, its source, a state switch (On, Name only, Off; Codex has On and Off; a plugin skill and Cursor have none) and the skill's note, one sentence on what its state means for the list (some skills have none). A press adds one `skill.rule` row to the tray; while the row waits, the pressed state shows a solid ring in the preview colour on the preview fill (`.ctx-switch button.pending`). The rule is the Library's, so Apply, backup, verify and Undo are unchanged.
 - **How this is counted.** A folded list under the picture: where the last list came from, the rule and the date it was checked, and what is not measured. It stays open across a redraw. Paths and log names live only here and in Details.
 - **Toast.** After Apply: "Applied 2 changes. The backup is in Changes. Your next chat will show the real list." with Undo ("Undo all" for two or more changes).
